A||||15||Back On Holiday||re-attaching plastic panels||||1||
Z||000000||Back On Holiday||10-07-2001||02:06 PM||||Question:  I have to replace the following,<BR>Dr side Frt. fender, dr side rocker panel,<BR>pass. side quarter panel.<BR>I already have the pieces, I was wondering if anybody else did replace them and what kind of gun and plastic rivets did you use to do it.  the dr side frt fender has 2 on the very bottom(besides that its a plug and play) and offhand I can't recall the other pieces since its been a few days since I removed them.  <P>I remember a post a few days ago about some guns, but they looked like only can be used for certain applications, I would like a gun that's cheap and does the job of all that stuff.  please...need help<P>advTHANKSance (Thanks in advance)<BR><P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||10-07-2001||02:32 PM||||When I put all the body panels back on my 84 I didn't use any rivets at all.  Instead I used small screws and nuts in the areas I could get to the backsides of, and screws and nutplates (aircraft parts) in areas where the backside is inaccessable.  Makes future dissassembly easier.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Back On Holiday||10-09-2001||08:06 PM||||Bump||||reg||1
Z||000003||MrPBody||10-09-2001||09:24 PM||||Ditto Rodrv6, more-or-less.  One rivet on front fender can be through-bolted.  I replaced all rivets on lower edge of rocker panel with black nylon license plate bolts, and replaced door sill rivets with black plastic screw rivets.  (Body-tite or similar.)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||skitime||10-09-2001||09:30 PM||||I found the best solution was a threaded insert gun.  It puts a permanent threaded nut into the sheetmetal so you can remove whenever necessary.  Tool is only 12.99 with some inserts too.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=1210" TARGET=_blank>http://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=1210</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||10-09-2001||09:47 PM||||I just installed a front fender,and the only thing I needed was a 1/4-20 nut/bolt for the very bottom of the panel.I either used some common screws or whatever was there before on the rest of it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Back On Holiday||10-10-2001||11:00 PM||||What about re-attaching the rocker panels through the holes under the sill pieces?  would that tool work with that?<P>any experience on re-attaching the rocker panels?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Back On Holiday||10-13-2001||10:05 AM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mickey_Moose||10-13-2001||11:34 AM||||The above meantioned will work anyplace - basically it installs a nut to the backside of the hole (via a rivet) - kind of like welding a nut to the backside of the hole, but way easier.<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Back On Holiday||10-13-2001||08:15 PM||||I'm going to order that tool right now.  thanks guys  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mach10||10-13-2001||08:30 PM||||Ski: that tool looks SWEET!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||SKIDMARK||10-13-2001||09:14 PM||||Slick tool Ski, I ordered one too. I was looking for the original fasteners and found out it would cost me about $250 for what I need to re-attach all the body panels. This gizmo should make it easy<P><BR>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport<p>[This message has been edited by SKIDMARK (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||skitime||10-13-2001||09:26 PM||||Only suggestion is buy inserts instead of use the ones on the kit.  The bought ones will be better quality but not cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Back On Holiday||10-14-2001||11:28 AM||||I ordered:<BR>1 2972-0VGA 9.99 NUT RIVETS (PACKAGE OF 100)<BR>1 1210-1VGA 12.99 45 PC. THREADED INSERT RIVETER KIT<BR>1 37964-3VGA 13.99 15 ft. x 20 ft. CUT SIZE BLUE OUTDOOR TARPAULIN<BR>1 43190-1VGA 29.99 1/4'' DRIVE SET, 3/8'' DRIVE SET, 1/2'' DRIVE SET <BR>PROFESSIONAL METRIC SOCKET SETS<P>Got the kit and a pkg of threaded nuts, also<BR>I need the tarp to close my small pool, and for 29.99, I got a metric socket set for spare sockets...: <A HREF="http://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=43190" TARGET=_blank>http://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=43190</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Smoooooth GT||10-14-2001||11:56 AM||||When doing some re-inforcing on the *Smoooth GT* I used 1 1/2" sheet metal screw's.. I used a piece of metal behind the piece that I was working on , and screwed through the piece and into the metal piece .. car is REAL TIGHT now...lol  It's also cheaper then buying a gun, rivet's, etc...  Just my 37 cent's worth..      Steve (the smooth one)<P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L V/6<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||3
